WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.820
- It's time for the first
reaction video of 2019.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.670
I'm excited, I just came
back from Costa Rica,

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:08.970
maybe you could notice the tan.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.686
Nurse Jackie Episode 1, Season 1.

00:00:11.686 --> 00:00:12.519
Be-whoop!

00:00:12.519 --> 00:00:15.602
(bright house music)

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.710
- [Jackie] What do you call
a nurse with a bad back?

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.760
Unemployed.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.351
- No!
- Ba-dum-bump.

00:00:22.351 --> 00:00:24.290
(laughs)

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.769
- Are those tomatoes?

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:28.630
(slow classic music)

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.290
Literally cherry tomatoes.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.374
I like cherry tomatoes.

00:00:32.374 --> 00:00:33.747
Nope, those are not cherry
tomatoes, she's doing lines.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.903
- [Jackie] Can you show me two fingers?

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.270
Peter, two fingers?

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.183
- Hey doc, you should get an iPhone.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.133
- You think so?

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:49.000
- All right this doctor's
absolutely awful,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.450
this doesn't happen in hospitals,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.120
if it does, people should be
losing their medical licenses.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:57.870
The patient is clearly mentally unstable,

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.650
or has some sort of altered mental status,

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:01.870
because he's in and out
of the conversation,

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.480
he can't hold up two fingers,

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.450
and his doctor is like,
checking his Blackberry

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.600
and talking about a vacation to St Barts.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.433
Come on bro!

00:01:08.433 --> 00:01:10.170
And first of all, who has a Blackberry?

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.321
I used to.

00:01:11.321 --> 00:01:12.640
- He's got a bleed, I'm
telling you right now.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.520
- [Doctor] He's totally lucid, 100%.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.950
Knock knock.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:16.820
- Who's there?

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:17.972
- See, what did I tell ya

00:01:17.972 --> 00:01:19.760
- (laughs) That's not how we determine

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.530
someone's neurological status.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:23.840
We do something known as
the Glasgow Coma Scale,

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.640
which gives you a score from 0-15,

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.200
depending on how alert you are.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.030
Besides that, we do a complete
neurological examination.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:33.250
We don't just look at someone,
make a knock knock joke,

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:34.815
and just assume they're good.

00:01:34.815 --> 00:01:38.480
(sad and gentle piano music)

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.383
- [Nurse] Acute Subdural Hematoma.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:44.680
The brain puffs up so fast,
it rips the blood vessels,

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.730
and you bleed to death inside your skull.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:48.850
- The skull is a closed environment,

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:50.360
and when you bleed into the skull,

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.470
that builds up extreme pressure,

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:55.740
now that pressure exhibits
what we call Mass Effect

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.820
onto the brain, and
puts even more pressure

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.710
and causes your brain cells to die.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:02.350
Horrible that this patient had
to loose his life like this,

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.220
for what, cause a doctor had an ego

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.420
and wanted to look cool
in front of the nurse?

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.490
- You should not have died.
- I agree

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:12.423
- Peter Michael Donovan.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.780
- Wait is she forging his organ donorship?

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.260
- It may be a shame but
it will not be a waste.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.900
- If she forged his
organ donor certificate

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.140
on the back of his license that's crazy.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.590
I have no words for that.

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:30.110
- We worked 911, not a scratch on us,

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:34.290
Peter's job is to ride a
bike, and he get's killed.

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:36.360
- Riding a bike is incredibly dangerous,

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.470
when I worked at a level 1 trauma center,

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.740
we would see bike accidents
happen all the time,

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:45.070
and unfortunately, many of
these people don't wear helmets,

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:47.320
and essentially, what
happens is they come in,

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:49.930
horrible brain bleed, and
its often too late for us

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.440
to even intervene in the hospital,

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.670
and they loose their lives.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.940
- I tell you to order a scan,
you order a goddamn scan,

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.270
because if you don't do it I'll
just go to the next doctor,

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:00.030
and the next doctor after
that, and in the mean time,

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.423
that kid died, and it is all on you.

00:03:04.731 --> 00:03:09.030
Wh- is this happening, not
happening I can't even tell.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:13.663
- Oh shit, oh crap, I-
I'm so sorry, oh God.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:16.200
No, when I get nervous I act out

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.393
with inappropriate sexual
touches, it's like turrets.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.550
- It's over, okay it
happened and now its over,

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.440
so there's that.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.770
I don't like chatty, okay, I
don't do chatty, I like quiet.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:29.270
Quiet and mean, those are my people.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:32.110
- I've worked with nurses
that were mean like this,

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.550
and I will say that secretly inside,

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:36.400
despite this mean exterior,

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.160
they have the biggest and sweetest hearts,

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:42.270
they care about people, and the
only reason they're so mean,

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.060
is because they wanna
protect their patients.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:45.910
They don't put up with nonsense,

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.862
so I defend you mean nurses.

00:03:47.862 --> 00:03:48.807
- [Jackie] We got you
inside, it's all right.

00:03:48.807 --> 00:03:50.400
- Got some John getting
off cutting up hookers

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.240
in the back of a limo,
dumped her in the alphabets.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:55.300
- Why did he have to cut me so bad?

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.140
- Did they get him?

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:58.150
- Nah, be on the lookout
for Vincent Van Gogh

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:00.041
and his fancy-fucking suit.

00:04:00.041 --> 00:04:02.350
She got the blade away from
him, cut his whole ear off.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:04.650
- Good girl, okay, put it on ice.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:07.460
- You never wanna take an organ like that

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:10.370
that is very sensitive and
put it directly on ice,

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:13.570
you wanna wrap it in a wet
cloth, and then put that on ice,

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:16.000
because the ice can
actually damage the tissue,

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.640
almost like creating frostbite.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.172
- [Nurse] Puke away from the ear Zoe.

00:04:20.172 --> 00:04:22.251
(laughs)

00:04:22.251 --> 00:04:24.418
(screams)

00:04:25.457 --> 00:04:27.707
(chuckles)

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:30.950
- Typical day in the hospital.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.810
- What do you doctors have
against healing people

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:33.727
for Christ sake?

00:04:33.727 --> 00:04:37.720
[Doctor] Ha, see that right
there, healing, helping,

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:39.713
fixing, it's fantastic.

00:04:40.827 --> 00:04:42.260
That's why you're a nurse.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.480
- I'm not digging the
stereotype right now.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:47.130
Doctors help people,
when we go get lunches

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.170
or dinners together,

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:49.980
we talk about what we
could have done better,

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.610
we try and learn from our cases,

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:54.250
so I'm taking this to heart right now,

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:57.560
and bad Nurse Jackie show writer.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.310
- 4 minutes til brain damage.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.580
- 2 til she passes out.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:03.373
- [Lady] Excuse me, we
need some help here.

00:05:05.153 --> 00:05:07.397
- [Jackie] I got it, you're buying lunch.

00:05:07.397 --> 00:05:09.397
(sighs)

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:13.610
(grunts)

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.690
- By doing the Heimlich
maneuver like that,

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.190
what you're doing is you're increasing

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:20.780
the inter abdominal pressure,
which then forces the air out,

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:22.810
therefore, helping you push out

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:25.350
whatever it is you are
choking on, or this poor lady

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:26.960
in this case, is choking on.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.280
- [Paramedic] 16 year old male,

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.930
shot a Roman candle out of his ass.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.100
- Third degree burns on his
scrotum and rectal area.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.563
- Oof, he put a firework in his butt?

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.651
- [Doctor] Can we close the door?

00:05:38.651 --> 00:05:41.620
(laughter)

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.410
- Never in my life have
I examined the patient,

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:48.380
let alone examined a patient in stirrups

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.710
with the door open like that, come on now.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:51.650
Come on now!

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.820
- I cannot even begin to imagine

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.730
what it must feel like
to be you right now.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:58.110
And I'm not going to cushion it,

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:00.760
and tell you I'm so sorry for your loss,

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.510
I know it is much bigger than that.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:07.383
But I am deeply, deeply sorry.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:12.913
But if its any comfort,
he's gonna be a hero now.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.930
His body is going to save lives.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:19.460
- That's actually an
incredibly good speech.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:22.780
Concise, easy to understand,
still apologetic,

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:24.070
without going too far.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.810
Except the fact that obviously she lied

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:28.960
and forged his organ donor signature.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:32.777
- Fine, can I have his heart?

00:06:32.777 --> 00:06:33.610
- Whoa!

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:35.343
- I'm sorry?

00:06:35.343 --> 00:06:36.176
- That took a turn.

00:06:36.176 --> 00:06:37.570
- Or how about a kidney?

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.240
I know there's like this organ market

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:41.930
where rich people buy, pay a
lot of money for body parts.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:44.027
- I know, it doesn't work that way.

00:06:44.027 --> 00:06:45.603
- $20,000 for a kidney.

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.460
Don't you think he owes me that?

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:51.840
For getting himself killed
on that goddamn bike.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:56.200
- A family member or girlfriend
of someone who just died.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.650
Give me one of his organs
so that I can sell it

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.070
on the Black Market, what?

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:02.480
- He made me pancakes this morning.

00:07:03.457 --> 00:07:05.157
- And you want to sell his kidney.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:11.350
You know what's funny, I've
never seen these pills before,

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:13.260
cause A I don't take them, and B

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:15.910
when I order them for my
patients I don't see them,

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:19.410
they pick them up either at the
pharmacy, or even at bedside

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.790
and the nurses brings them to the patient,

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.450
so I've never seen these pills.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:24.790
What doctors have, is
we have some great apps,

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.480
like Epocrates, that we
can open, get information

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.490
about the medications we're giving.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:32.220
You can check the dosing, the formulary,

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.030
adverse reactions, drug interactions,

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:36.200
but then you go click
here for pill pictures,

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.520
and you could see, but
none of these look like

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.140
the ones she was using.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.603
What about OxyContin.

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:45.300
Pill pictures... none of these are red.

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:48.230
Oh, oh, these kinda look like
what she was using right?

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:52.080
- That woman you cut took 287 stitches

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:53.703
and 10 pints of blood.

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:56.600
- [Patient] She liked to cut herself.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:57.970
- Oh it was her idea?

00:07:57.970 --> 00:08:01.803
- Yes, American women
are very adventurous.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.593
- She probably did it for attention.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.333
- What do you do for attention?

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:11.743
- I'll be right back.

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.239
(beep) you.

00:08:16.239 --> 00:08:18.322
(laughs)

00:08:19.993 --> 00:08:21.082
(flushing)

00:08:21.082 --> 00:08:24.423
- I could have saved that
boy, that messenger kid.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:26.990
I knew there was a bleed, I felt it.

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:29.070
- This is where we need to use this

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.640
as a learning opportunity
to create a system

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:34.460
in their hospital, like my hospital has,

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.690
where anyone, whether you're a nurse,

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:39.700
part of the janitorial
staff, doctor, resident,

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:42.109
can report an error like this,

00:08:42.109 --> 00:08:44.600
that needs to be investigated by the staff

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.988
so it doesn't happen again, and even if,

00:08:46.988 --> 00:08:48.700
let's say they had a good outcome,

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:51.000
and she still felt like
she wasn't being heard,

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:54.020
she needs to come on to
that system and report

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:56.650
what we call a near miss,
and a near miss is when

00:08:56.650 --> 00:08:59.440
a mistake almost happens,
even though you catch it,

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:01.554
but you still use it as
a learning opportunity

00:09:01.554 --> 00:09:04.150
so that a near miss
doesn't even happen again.

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:06.390
- Do you think there's
a finite amount of pain

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:07.283
in the world?

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.430
Like if I take the thorn
out of someone's hand,

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:12.880
does that pain have to go somewhere else?

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:15.193
- Yes, that's why there's drugs.

00:09:15.193 --> 00:09:17.640
- (laughs) No, disagree

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:22.273
- I think you're a
Saint, just so you know.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.750
(shuffling)

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:28.070
- I like her bunny scrubs, I'm jealous,

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:29.877
I want a pair like that.

00:09:29.877 --> 00:09:32.552
(beeping)

00:09:32.552 --> 00:09:34.885
(scuffling)

00:09:39.674 --> 00:09:42.174
- Dammit, I almost killed you.

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:46.880
- That's why we don't
take drugs on the job.

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:48.980
It's pretty funny but
it looks like those bags

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:53.410
are just saline, so I don't
know how she almost killed him,

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.520
but it doesn't look like it.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.550
That's what we call a
near miss by the way.

00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:59.130
- Wanna come over tonight?

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.203
- Not tonight okay?

00:10:02.255 --> 00:10:04.563
- I brought you something for your back.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:07.933
- Doctor Pepper.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:16.373
Moon pie, I was thinking more
along the lines of Vicodin.

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:20.060
- There's actually been a lot of scandals,

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:25.060
with doctors and pharmacists
either overprescribing

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:28.380
narcotics, or maybe even getting
caught stealing narcotics,

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:31.920
now, they're locked up in these machines.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.870
In my hospital they're
called Pyxis machines,

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:35.950
where you need to
actively get fingerprints,

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:38.780
they'll scan your badge in
order to get any kind of

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.290
number of medications out.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:42.470
Also there's been a lot of
doctors where I come from

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:46.410
in Brooklyn, that have
been arrested and charged

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:49.910
with distributing these
narcotics because they were just

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:52.710
writing scripts for patients nonstop,

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:55.690
100 pills, 100 pills, unlimited refills.

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:58.870
Those who haven't yet been caught, be wary

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:01.003
because we are coming for you.

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:04.774
- Be careful.

00:11:04.774 --> 00:11:05.780
- (beep) you

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:08.743
- Whoa, welcome to New York.

00:11:13.443 --> 00:11:16.260
(puncturing)

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:17.630
How did he not catch that?

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:20.680
No joke, I am a fan of Nurse Jackie.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.110
It's not a doctor show,

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.160
but there's enough medical stuff

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.570
for me to comment on for sure.

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:27.260
If you want a funny video,
check out my bloopers.

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:28.680
Click it, I know you wanna.

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:29.913
Stay happy and healthy.

